We use the built-in id function to compare the identity of the input_array with the visited set of ids, to detect circular references. If an input_array's id is in the visited set, we return an empty set to avoid an infinite recursion. Otherwise, we add the id to the visited set.

The function works by first checking the data type of the input. If the data type is list, dictionary, or set, it recursively calls itself on the sub-items until it reaches the base case, which is when it encounters a non-list, non-dictionary, non-set item. At that point, it adds the item to the set and returns the set.

